{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Change 2723 is double-green; local `make verify` is blocked by an unrelated host defect\n\nGerrit change: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2723\n`LLM-Review +1` (rebar review bot) and `Verified +1` (rebar CI bot), 0 unresolved\ncomments, `submittable: true`. Not submitted — left for the operator.\n\n### Local `make verify` — what actually happened\n\nThree runs on this host, same commit: lint and typecheck green every time\n(including the complexity and mechanism-delta ratchets), and 19,873-19,884 tests\npassing. Every failure in every run was\n`GateCongestedError: gate admission refused: all 4 concurrent slots busy`, with a\nDIFFERENT failure set each run (15 / 9 / 26).\n\nRoot cause is NOT this change. `make test` runs pytest `-n 4`, and the gate\nadmission cap is 4 slots that are HOST-GLOBAL — `_slot_dir()`\n(`src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py:210`) puts them under the snapshot store root's\n`locks/`, shared by every rebar process on the box. During one run the holder was\ncaptured directly:\n\n    60942 /Users/joeoakhart/scanner-promote/.venv/bin/rebar review-plan\n          guileless-emeritus-izuthrush\n\n— another worktree's plan review. Each affected test passes when run alone, and\nthe same multi-file selection passes on unmodified `main`. Filed as\n`careful-liberal-skua` (e5eb-ef5e-c10a-4729), linked `discovered_from` this\nticket.\n\nCI's `Verified +1` on this exact commit — an isolated runner with no competing\nrebar processes — is the authoritative signal that the suite is green.\n\n### Scope note\n\nThe fix caches the resolver index PER PROCESS. A long-lived process (the MCP\nserver) pays one store pass and then resolves for free; a one-shot CLI invocation\nstill pays that pass once, though `show_ticket` benefits immediately because it\nresolves twice per call. Persisting the index ACROSS processes would also help\none-shot CLI use and is deliberately not attempted here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788670187388305001,"uuid":"a8db8d62-b19e-452a-8ffb-a45bdbb5a6eb"}